run: /Users/cmatsoukis/Desktop/Apps/experiment-1/runs/bench-watchlist/wl-sort+governor@6000-01
provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: In the watchlist, show movies I haven't watched yet before the ones I've watched.

governor turn 1: plan -> watchlist  (Request is purely a watchlist display-order change: sort unwatched before watched. Targeting only the watchlist component's `movies` signal (stable unwatched-first partition of store items) keeps watchlist-store and all other consumers untouched, needs no interface change, and the acceptance test pins both signal order and DOM order, including reactive re-ordering on toggle/remove.)
round 1: owners watchlist=rejected; oracle RED
governor turn 2: plan -> watchlist  (The watchlist submission was rejected only because two existing tests use index-based DOM lookups that assume store order; the requested unwatched-first ordering necessarily sinks a just-toggled-to-watched movie, so the owner's minimal checkbox-index adaptations preserve those tests' intent and I approve them. Separately, one oracle failure was in my own acceptance test: the Watchlist template's RouterLink needs ActivatedRoute, which an empty TestBed doesn't provide (NG0201) — fixed by adding provideRouter([]). The remaining assertion failure simply reflects that the watchlist change has not been applied yet, so I re-issue the plan.)
round 2: owners watchlist=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 3: accept  (Oracle is green (tsc clean, 32/32 tests pass). The watchlist component now partitions store items unwatched-first with a stable, reactive order (add/remove/toggle all update immediately) and the template renders through the movies signal, verified by the acceptance tests. The two pre-existing checkbox/row-click tests were adapted only in their index-based lookup, as approved last round, with intent intact.)

